A future count-based mass pool (e.g. larvae_count) would be silently missed by structural coverage tests. Adding a doc comment or suffix convention check is low-risk and prevents a real class of future silent omission."},{"amendment_id":"fr-8-1415e3ec","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: water_change.rs line 60 applies `dissolved_feed_residue_g_total *= retention` but this reduction is absent from the nitrogen/carbon export delta calculations at lines 109-118. No existing comment explains the omission. Since the residue counter mirrors DOC/DON already tracked in the budget, adding it to the delta would double-count. A clarifying comment is zero-risk and prevents a future developer from mistakenly including it."},{"amendment_id":"fr-8-2fe7314b","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: Both test_total_n_helper_sums_all_pools (line 291) and test_total_c_helper_sums_all_pools (line 319) sum particulate_organics_g_total + fine_detritus_g_total before passing to a single conversion function. This exploits linearity and would not detect a bug where different conversion formulas or N:C ratios are assigned to particulate vs. fine detritus. Computing the two contributions separately is trivial and improves test sensitivity."},{"amendment_id":"fr-8-8959bb9b","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: In plant_growth.rs:157, route_plant_loss_to_dissolved_organics sends respiration losses directly to dissolved_organic_nitrogen and dissolved_organic_carbon (lines 391-392). In algae_growth.rs, route_algae_loss_to_dissolved_organics does the same (lines 284-285), and respiration+grazing are lumped together before routing (lines 117-122). Default DIC rates at process.rs:227-228 are both 0.0, confirming no O2 consumption or DIC production occurs. Senescence IS correctly routed to fine_detritus (plant_growth.rs:158-159). The respiration pathway is biologically wrong — it should produce DIC/CO2 and consume O2, not generate DON/DOC. This is a genuine modeling error even though the budget closes numerically."},{"amendment_id":"fr-8-65a8127d","decision":"reject","rationale":"Factually incorrect. Verified fund_live_shrimp_biomass (shrimp.rs:636-648): it checks only animal.reserve_g and returns false if insufficient. There is no fallback to dissolved_organic_nitrogen, ammonia_total, dissolved_organic_carbon, or dissolved_inorganic_carbon. The function is 13 lines of straightforward reserve-check logic with no water-column nutrient access. The call sites at hatching (line 629-634) and maturation (lines 545-554) both correctly handle the false return by not creating/maturing shrimp. The described biological pathway issue does not exist in the current code."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0aee66ff-909b-46da-9b35-34277f86d5cc"}
